# Review of entity joins that rest on too little evidence.
#
# A record that joins an entity on very few matching rules is about as likely
# to be a wrong merge as a real match. Such a join is recorded as a review
# case, which an actor claims, decides and thereby either confirms or splits
# apart again.
#
# Claiming a case locks the affected entity, so that its data cannot change
# while it is being decided. The lock is released when the case is resolved or
# released again.
#
# A type extension cannot carry a description, hence the plain comment.

extend type Query {
  """ReviewCases returns a page of the review queue, oldest case first."""
  reviewCases(input: ReviewCasesInput): ReviewCasesOutput! @hasPrivilege(privilege: "tilores/query.reviewCases")

  """ReviewDecisions returns the decisions that earlier involved any of the
provided records, newest decision first.

The history is asked for by records rather than by entity, because an entity ID
may have merged away since a decision was made while a record ID is permanent.
Pass the records of an entity to get the history of that entity."""
  reviewDecisions(input: ReviewDecisionsInput!): ReviewDecisionsOutput! @hasPrivilege(privilege: "tilores/query.reviewDecisions")
}

extend type Mutation {
  """CreateReviewCase puts an entity into the review queue that the automatic
detection never flagged.

The case carries no links, because there was no detection that could have found
them. Which of the entity's links are wrong is what the review establishes, and
resolveReviewCase accepts a verdict for any pair of records.

Asking twice for the same entity returns the case that is already waiting
instead of queueing a second one for the same thing."""
  createReviewCase(input: CreateReviewCaseInput!): CreateReviewCaseOutput! @hasPrivilege(privilege: "tilores/mutation.createReviewCase")

  """ClaimReviewCase takes a case out of the queue and locks its entity for the
provided actor.

The returned entity is resolved from the records of the case and may differ
from the entity the case was created for. A case whose records no longer exist
or no longer share a single entity is reported as stale and nothing is
locked."""
  claimReviewCase(input: ClaimReviewCaseInput!): ClaimReviewCaseOutput! @hasPrivilege(privilege: "tilores/mutation.claimReviewCase")

  """ReleaseReviewCase unlocks the entity of a claimed case and puts the case
back into the queue without deciding it.

The entity and the lock only need to be provided when the case itself no longer
exists, which is how a lock is recovered after a client crashed."""
  releaseReviewCase(input: ReleaseReviewCaseInput!): ReleaseReviewCaseOutput! @hasPrivilege(privilege: "tilores/mutation.releaseReviewCase")

  """ResolveReviewCase decides a claimed case.

Every link of the case must be decided, one by one, and further links of the
same entity may be decided along with them. The rejected links are removed by a
disassembly, which happens asynchronously, so a triggered resolution has been
enqueued rather than applied. Keeping some links of a candidate while rejecting
others leaves the entity joined by the kept ones. The decision itself is kept
permanently."""
  resolveReviewCase(input: ResolveReviewCaseInput!): ResolveReviewCaseOutput! @hasPrivilege(privilege: "tilores/mutation.resolveReviewCase")
}

"""ReviewCasesInput selects the part of the review queue to return."""
input ReviewCasesInput @goModel(model: "github.com/tilotech/tilores-plugin-api/dispatcher.ReviewCasesInput") {
